{
  "_comment": "The model catalog shipped with each Spark Swapper release. Every entry names the platforms it runs on, how to install it, how to start/stop it and the speeds its recipe publishes. {{USER}}, {{HOME}}, {{API_KEY}} and {{API_PORT}} are filled in from the site config (/etc/spark-swapper/models.json, openclaw.user / openclaw.home, api_key, api_port); {{NAME}} for a name under \"snippets\" is replaced by that text. A model with the same key in the site config is merged over the catalog entry field by field (the site wins); list a key in the site config's \"hidden_models\" to hide it. Speeds are tokens per second: decode = one request on its own, decode_concurrent = the total across `concurrency` requests. \"footprint\" names what a model leaves on the disk besides what its install steps make (dirs, hf repos, images, shared_images): the Storage tab measures it and Delete removes it, keeping whatever another installed model still uses. \"profiles\" are the engine templates behind Add from Hugging Face; \"builds\" are Dockerfiles for images built on the box.",

